From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: Poll for directory changes on the PS5.

The server reports directory changes (FindFirstChangeNotification,
ReadDirectoryChangesW, NtNotifyChangeDirectoryFile) through inotify, and
the console has no inotify, dnotify or kqueue, so a watch never fired.
Poll a watched directory instead: its entries (the whole subtree when the
subtree is watched) are listed with file identity, size and times and
compared with the previous list, and what differs is reported as inotify
would: names that appeared or went, a rename (a name that went and one
with the same file identity that came, with a cookie), a file whose size
or times changed. A watch that takes long to list is polled less often,
from 25 ms up to 2 s between two lists. From PS5_Proton (mihawk-99, its
patch 0902), rebased onto this tree.

  server/change.c | 281 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
  server/fd.c     |   5 +
  server/file.h   |   1 +
  3 files changed, 287 insertions(+)

